Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OpenXT]

Keep alternative-call ops tables mapped after init

GCC 15 materializes alternative_call()'s unused "g"(func) input as a
RIP-relative load of the ops table.  With ALTERNATIVE_CALL and without
LIVEPATCH, that table is __initdata and is unmapped after boot, so the
extra load page-faults in do_memory_op via xsm_ops.

Always use __ro_after_init, as the livepatch build already does.

--- a/xen/include/xen/alternative-call.h
+++ b/xen/include/xen/alternative-call.h
@@ -52,12 +52,13 @@
 
 #include <asm/alternative-call.h>
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_LIVEPATCH
-/* Must keep for livepatches to resolve alternative calls. */
-# define __alt_call_maybe_initdata __ro_after_init
-#else
-# define __alt_call_maybe_initdata __initdata
-#endif
+/*
+ * Must stay mapped after boot.  LIVEPATCH needs the table for later
+ * resolution.  GCC 15 also emits a RIP-relative load of the table
+ * beside the alternative_call site, which page-faults if the object
+ * was discarded with .init.data.
+ */
+# define __alt_call_maybe_initdata __ro_after_init
 
 /*
  * Devirtualise the alternative_{,v}call()'s on boot.  Convert still-NULL
